 * The app's own UI, declared as the first plugin (docs/ui-plugins.md).
 * Everything here is data the registries read; the React that serves the
 * settings sections is bound in ./index.ts. Parsing at module load means a
 * malformed built-in manifest fails the first render and the unit test,
 * never a user's session.
 *
 * Card kinds: the four wire kinds of cards.ts (decision D-9), plus the
 * host-owned `task-record` (task-system P4). The chrome and body policy
 * that used to be three switch statements in the card layer live here as
 * rows. `task-result` streams as linked plain text (a report mid-flight);
 * everything else renders its frame from the first byte. Only the live
 * prototype gets the interactive sanitizer profile. `task-record` is NOT a
 * wire kind: it is never persisted in `cards` and never emitted by an agent
 * (`cardKindSchema` refuses it), so its body policy is moot - the body is
 * a template the host mounts for the open task (./record).
 *
 * Side panels (phase 2): the activity feed and the crew strip ride the left
 * rail as Tier-2 frames - the dogfood the proposal named, and the streaming
 * probe. The right rail carries the now panel (P4): what IS, minimal by
 * default, the one panel the captain chose for it (decision D3).
